se,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"### Describe the bug\n\nI'm getting duplicated index objects in the `MetaData` when using `DeferredReflection`.\r\n\r\nI think a similar issue might've been fixed in https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/3861.\r\n\r\nSimilar problem has been reported in https://stackoverflow.com/questions/55271904/sqlalchemy-with-multiple-databases-and-error-due-to-duplicate-index-creation.\r\n\r\n\n\n### To Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom sqlalchemy.ext.declarative import DeferredReflection, declarative_base\r\nfrom sqlalchemy import Column, DateTime, String, Table\r\nfrom sqlalchemy import create_engine\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.sql import text\r\n\r\n\r\n# Create a new database\r\nengine = create_engine(\"sqlite:///:memory:\")\r\nwith engine.connect() as conn:\r\n    conn.execute(text(\"CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS foo (id varchar, created_at datetime);\"))\r\n    conn.execute(text(\"CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS ix_foo_created_at ON foo (created_at);\"))\r\n\r\n\r\n# Now use the deferred reflection mechanism to reflect the table in Python\r\nBase = declarative_base(bind=engine)\r\n\r\n\r\nclass Foo(DeferredReflection, Base):\r\n    __table__ = Table(\r\n        \"foo\",\r\n        Base.metadata,\r\n        Column(\"id\", String(1024), primary_key=True),\r\n        Column(\"created_at\", DateTime, index=True),\r\n        extend_existing=True,\r\n    )\r\n\r\n\r\n# Should be one index -> OK!\r\nassert len(Base.metadata.tables[\"foo\"].indexes) == 1\r\n\r\nFoo.prepare(engine)\r\n\r\n# Still only one index expected, whoops!\r\nassert len(Base.metadata.tables[\"foo\"].indexes) == 1, Base.metadata.tables[\"foo\"].indexes\n```\n\n\n### Error\n\n```\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"dup_test.py\", line 34, in <module>\r\n    assert len(Base.metadata.tables[\"foo\"].indexes) == 1, Base.metadata.tables[\"foo\"].indexes\r\nAssertionError: {Index('ix_foo_created_at', Column('created_at', DateTime(), table=<foo>)), Index('ix_foo_created_at', Column('created_at', DateTime(), table=<foo>))}\r\n````\n\n### Versions\n\n- OS: Mac OS\r\n- Python: 3.6.13\r\n- SQLAlchemy: 1.4.26\r\n- Database: SQLite\r\n- DBAPI (eg: psycopg, cx_oracle, mysqlclient): sqlite3\r\n\n\n### Additional context\n\n_No response_","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/7366/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/7366/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]